# UI Guidelines

## General

- UI doesn't contain business logic.
- Business logic is delegated to viewmodel.
- Try to prefer where possible widget `const` and `Stateless` 

## Pages

- Every Page file must be called <feature_name>_page.dart
- Every Page widget name must start with **Runaya** word
  - Example: *lib/registration/application/ux/pages/registration_verify_email_page.dart*
- For every page use as start widget the **RunayaPage**. It is a custom page with custom transition and lifecycle.
  - Example: *lib/registration/application/ux/pages/registration_verify_email_page.dart*

## Widgets

- Every widget name must start with **Runaya** word
  - Example: *lib/core/application/ux/widgets/textfield_widget.dart*
- Specific feature widget must be insert in the feature folder itself.
- Shared or reusable components from 2 or more features must be insert in the **lib/core/application/ux**

## Composition

- Try to have always small and reusable widget.
- Keep the `build()` method under ~30 lines (ideal).
- If it exceeds 50-60 lines, extract sub-widgets into dedicated files.
- Each extracted widget should have a single visual responsibility.
- No unnecessary `setState()` or provider rebuilds
- Images use proper caching (`CachedNetworkImage` or similar)
- Lists use `ListView.builder` instead of `ListView(children: [...])` for long lists
- No rebuilds of entire widget trees — use `const`, `select`, or granular providers

## Style and Theme

- Don't use hardcoded colors or style.
  - All the colors must be insert in *lib/core/application/ux/theme/color.dart*
  - All the theme component must be insert in lib/core/application/ux/theme/theme.dart
- For the Design component try to generalize it in the *ThemeData*. If is not possible or there are limitations, create a custom widget. 
  - Example: **Custom Textfield** in *lib/core/application/ux/widgets/textfield_widget.dart* with the basic design in  **InputDecorationTheme** in *lib/core/application/ux/theme/color.dart*

## Responsive

- Try to not use fixed pixel value for dimension. Use it only in exceptional cases.

## Best Pattern

- Try to use the loading, error and success state of riverpod for the UI where is possible.
  - There are *lib/core/application/ux/widgets/shimmer_loading_widget.dart* and *lib/core/application/ux/widgets/overlay_loading_widget.dart* for loading state
  - There are *lib/core/application/ux/widgets/dialog_widget.dart* and *lib/core/application/ux/widgets/snackbar_widget.dart* for the error.
  - Example: *lib/registration/application/ux/pages/registration_verify_email_page.dart*
